  "notes": "Drawn from 737 MAX 8s HL8594 (2026-06-12, right), HL8523 (2026-06-04, left from below) and HL8524 (2026-02-04). The same scheme is worn by the 737-800s. The engine cowls carry 'www.jejuair.net' in orange on the white (not drawn as a title). The orange band's underside: the belly centerline looks white with the wordmark on it in HL8523 (partly hidden by the engine), so the band is drawn as a lower-side stripe only. No dedicated logo symbol: Jeju Air's logo is its wordmark, drawn as titles. Re-checked 2026-11-15: drawn for the 737-800 (the commonest type; the MAX 8 photographed has the same fuselage); the wordmark's lowercase 'air' measured at 0.75 of its capitals (HL8523); the fin's discs are circles and the band's edges curves, now drawn smooth.",
  "history": "Replaced Skyarium v1's approximation. Jeju Air's scheme since its 2006 start, the dotted tail added in a later refresh (date not confirmed)."
}
